ous miracles at this sacred site. On all auspicious occasions such as consecrations and shantisnatra ceremonies everywhere, the mantra-syllables of Shri Jiravala Parshwanathji are inscribed — a true testament to the Lord's power.\\\"}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Devout Jains recall and pay homage to this pilgrimage site every morning and evening in the tirtha-vandana sutra recited during pratikraman. Every year a fair is held here on Kartik Purnima, Chaitra Purnima, and the fifth day of the bright half of Bhadrapad.\\\"}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Inscriptions at Arbudachal (Mount Abu) also prove that Shraman Bhagwan Shri Mahavir himself set foot upon Arbudachal. During this period, Jirapalli Tirth had already gained renown as a fully consecrated pilgrimage site. The Sakal Tirth Vandana Stotra also glorifies this pilgrimage site with the line \\\\\\\"Jiravalo ne Thambhan Pas.\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Various inscriptions, dedicatory prashastis, and colophons (pushpikas) provide evidence that this great pilgrimage site underwent renovation and re-consecration over many centuries. Renovations and consecrations took place in the 4th, 8th, 12th, and 16th centuries of the Vikram era, and strong evidence exists of extensive renovation and construction work in the 18th and 19th centuries as well.\\\"}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"13\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"A major recurring cause for these repeated renovations was the Mughal invasions. Since the Marudhar region formed the western frontier of Aryavarta, our pilgrimage sites and temples were the first to suffer damage from the attacks of fanatical foreign powers. These zealots demolished temples and defaced images, but they could never destroy the faith rooted in people's hearts. As a result, the pilgrimage site was rebuilt again and again through the selfless dedication of the faithful. Following the wise counsel of the earlier acharyas, our ancestors combined whatever limited means were available to them with their faith, undertaking a Herculean effort to preserve intact the glory of the Lord's image and his abode. It is by virtue of that effort that we are blessed with the presence of this deity even today.\\\"}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"14\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: There is one other temple.\\\"}]\\n2d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"15\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Art and Sculpture: The natural scenery of this secluded spot amid the hills in the forest is extremely beautiful, peaceful, and captivating.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/page,_N_T_/en/tirtha/tirtha-090"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug","/$d$lang/tirtha","/$d$lang","/_index","/_head"],"revalidate":60,"cacheControl":{"revalidate":60,"expire":31536000}}}